// Relativization / partition-safety, `previous` operator, keyed by RESOURCE.
//
// A Read is permitted iff THIS resource's immediately preceding own event
// (within 1h) was a Login. The event schema pins `callerResource` universally
// (see event.dwschema), so `previous` means "this resource's previous event",
// not "the previous event in the global trace".
//
// The principal is held constant (alice) across every event, so ONLY the
// resource pin distinguishes "mine" from "foreign". The differential pair for
// alice's Read on gw1 at @3:
//   trace_1: alice Login on gw1, alice Transfer on GW2 (foreign resource), alice Read on gw1.
//   trace_2: alice Login on gw1,                                            alice Read on gw1.
// Under resource-local semantics the gw2 Transfer is invisible to gw1, so
// gw1's previous own event is the Login in BOTH traces → PERMIT in both. Under
// (incorrect) global semantics — or a bug that keyed on principal (alice is the
// same everywhere) — trace_1's previous event would be the gw2 Transfer → deny,
// diverging from trace_2. The resource pin is what excludes it.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    previous within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
